\chapter{Ownership-aware container libraries}
\label{ch:60}
\index{Ownership-aware container libraries}

\OnxCodeTerm{Box}, \OnxCodeTerm{Cell}, \OnxCodeTerm{Local}, and \OnxCodeTerm{Quarantine} implement focused policies using checked owners and lexical borrows. \OnxCodeTerm{Rc} and \OnxCodeTerm{Arc} cover admitted strong shared owners, while \OnxCodeTerm{RefCell} adds local dynamic borrow guards. The native \OnxCodeTerm{Tls} and \OnxCodeTerm{Foreign} modules link special companion sources. \OnxCodeTerm{Pod} is the supervised fixed worker profile, with separate authorization and host limits.

\begin{OnxCodeBlock}[numbers=none]
import std.container.Box as B;
fn main()
{
  let owner = B.basis_box_new(42);
  assert(B.basis_box_into_inner(move(owner)) == 42);
}
\end{OnxCodeBlock}

The extraction consumes the Box. Add a separate negative case that tries to extract from the same binding twice. For a dynamic guard, test that an incompatible borrow fails and that a later valid borrow can succeed after guard release. The bounded native operations on Arc do not grant arbitrary cross-thread closure or payload transfer. Verify each native container with the intended link and runtime profile.

